<div class="mh-row clearfix">
	<div id="main-content" class="mh-content"><article class="post-wrapper post-199779 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-aew-tv-reviews category-mustreadarticles category-newsticker category-tv_reports tag-aew tag-aew-collision tag-aew-dynamite tag-alex-shelley tag-austin-creed tag-bandido tag-brody-king tag-cash-wheeler tag-chris-sabin tag-dax-harwood tag-jay-white tag-jon-moxley tag-kofi tag-kyle-fletcher tag-marina-shafir tag-mercedes-mone tag-mike-bailey tag-stokely-hathaway tag-tommaso-ciampa tag-will-ospreay">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">
			AEW Dynamite and Collision results (11/11): Powell&#8217;s live review of the Full Gear go-home block with Will Ospreay and Kyle Fletcher, FTR vs. MCMG in the fifth match of the best-of-five series		</h1><p class="entry-meta">
<span class="entry-meta-date updated"><i class="fa fa-clock-o"></i>November 11, 2026</span></p>
    </header><div class="widget_text post-ad-widget widget_custom_html"><div class="textwidget custom-html-widget"><div id="FreeStarVideoAdContainer">
<div id="freestar-video-parent">
<div id="freestar-video-child"></div>
	</div>
</div>

<!-- Tag ID: prowrestling_incontent_1 -->
<div align="center" data-freestar-ad="__336x280 __336x280" id="prowrestling_incontent_1">
<script data-cfasync="false" type="text/javascript">
    freestar.config.enabled_slots.push({ placementName: "prowrestling_incontent_1", slotId: "prowrestling_incontent_1" });
  </script>
</div></div></div><p class="entry-category">
<span class="entry-category-title">Categories</span><a href="https://prowrestling.net/site/category/tv_reports/aew-tv-reviews/" rel="category tag">AEW TV REVIEWS</a> <a href="https://prowrestling.net/site/category/mustreadarticles/" rel="category tag">MUST-READ LIST</a> <a href="https://prowrestling.net/site/category/newsticker/" rel="category tag">NEWS TICKER</a> <a href="https://prowrestling.net/site/category/tv_reports/" rel="category tag">TV REVIEWS</a></p>
	<div class="entry-content">
		<div id="prowr-580628369" class="prowr-apple-podcast-button-link prowr-entity-placement" style="margin-left: auto;margin-right: auto;text-align: center;" role="region" aria-label="Advertisements"><a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/pro-wrestling-boom-podcast/id1365989370" aria-label="SUBSCRIBE IN APPLE PODCASTS"><img decoding="async" src="https://i0.wp.com/prowrestling.net/site/wp-content/uploads/advanced_ads/2019/07/Logo2019_ApplePodcasts_320wide.png?fit=320%2C78&#038;ssl=1" alt="SUBSCRIBE IN APPLE PODCASTS"  srcset="https://i0.wp.com/prowrestling.net/site/wp-content/uploads/advanced_ads/2019/07/Logo2019_ApplePodcasts_320wide.png?w=320&ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/prowrestling.net/site/wp-content/uploads/advanced_ads/2019/07/Logo2019_ApplePodcasts_320wide.png?resize=300%2C73&ssl=1 300w" sizes="(max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px" width="320" height="78"   /></a></div><p><strong>By Jason Powell</strong>, ProWrestling.net Editor (<a href="https://twitter.com/prowrestlingnet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@prowrestlingnet</a>)</p>
<p><b>AEW Dynamite (Episode 371) and AEW Collision (Episode 170)<br />
November 11, 2026, in West Valley City, Utah, at Maverik Center</b><br />
<b>Simulcast live on TBS and HBO Max</b></p>
<p><strong>[Hour One]</strong> Pyro shot off on the stage. Excalibur checked in from the broadcast table with Nigel McGuinness and Tony Schiavone. They ran through some of the matches for tonight&#8217;s show and Saturday&#8217;s AEW Full Gear pay-per-view. They added Queen Aminata vs. Skye Blue vs. Hyan in a three-way for the TBS Championship, and the Young Bucks and Jack Perry vs. three Don Callis members in a trios match to tonight&#8217;s card&#8230; A video package recapped last week&#8217;s Blood &amp; Guts matches&#8230;</p>
<p>Schiavone set up footage aired from after last week&#8217;s Blood &amp; Guts match, which he said they captured because he was going to interview Will Ospreay. The footage showed Ospreay speaking with Adam Copeland in the locker room while Steven Borden, Matt Jackson, and Nick Jackson listened. Ospreay was upset with Copeland for surrendering. Copeland got upset and defended his decision while talking about his neck surgery, Ospreay&#8217;s neck surgery, and how he feels in the morning. Copeland exited the room, while the others tried to call him back&#8230;</p>
<p>Kyle Fletcher made his entrance with Don Callis. AEW World Champion Will Ospreay made his entrance for the face-to-face meeting. Fletcher wore a suit, while Ospreay wore jeans and a T-shirt. Fletcher called for Ospreay&#8217;s music to be cut off while Ospreay was playing to the crowd. The fans chanted &#8220;you look stupid&#8221; to Fletcher, who responded, &#8220;No, I don&#8217;t.&#8221;</p>
<p>Fletcher recalled standing in the ring in the same venue three years earlier and shaving his head. Fletcher said Ospreay has had quite the run since then, pointing to Ospreay undergoing neck surgery, getting married, and coming back and winning the AEW World Championship. Fletcher said he&#8217;s won the TNT Title twice, been an AEW Trios Champion, and an AEW International Champion since then. Fletcher said he knows none of that would have happened had it not been for Ospreay. Fletcher thanked Ospreay.</p>
<p>Ospreay said he didn&#8217;t expect this type of encounter after what happened the week before. He said the words meant a lot ot him, and he thanked him. Ospreay said he&#8217;s kept an eye on Fletcher for two years, and he&#8217;s very proud of him. Ospreay said he hoped that Fletcher could say the same to him. Fletcher cut him off and accused him of twisting his words. Fletcher said he wouldn&#8217;t change anything, including stabbing Ospreay&#8217;s head with a screwdriver and dropping him on his head with a Tiger Driver.</p>
<p>Fletcher questioned Ospreay for seeking retribution after returning from neck surgery by going after Jon Moxley. Fletcher wanted Ospreay to give him credit for breaking his neck. Ospreay said it was true that Fletcher was responsible for the most excruciating ten months of his life. Ospreay recalled working through the pain because he was in the first year of his AEW contract, and he didn&#8217;t want to let anyone down. Ospreay said the only reason he got through it was that the fans would hear the opening to his entrance theme and lose their minds. He said the fans in Fletcher&#8217;s home country even cheered him.</p>
<p>Ospreay said Fletcher shouldn&#8217;t brag too much about breaking his neck because he beat him twice before he had surgery. Ospreay said he&#8217;s 100 percent now and questioned if Fletcher actually thinks he has a chance. Ospreay spoke of performing a Black Arrow when the world needed it most, and beating Kenny Omega to win the championship. Ospreay said he sent in a clip that he wanted played on the big screen so that he could get Fletcher&#8217;s reaction.</p>
<p>Footage aired from AEW All In London of Ospreay&#8217;s walk through the backstage area before he made his entrance. It included Ospreay walking past Fletcher and Mark Davis. Ospreay told Fletcher to tell him what he was feeling at that moment. Fletcher claimed he felt &#8220;absolutely nothing.&#8221; Ospreay accused him of lying. Ospreay said he thought Fletcher saw someone he still loved deep down and wanted to be ringside with him, just like in old times. Fletcher got fired up and said he felt jealous. Fletcher said he had to watch the man he hates most in the world achieve the dream he had for himself. Fletcher said the feeling didn&#8217;t last long because he realized that he could be the man who takes it all away from Ospreay.</p><div id="prowr-59042031" class="prowr-content-4 prowr-entity-placement" role="region" aria-label="Advertisements"><!-- Tag ID: prowrestling_incontent_2 -->
<div align="center" data-freestar-ad="__336x280 __336x280" id="prowrestling_incontent_2">
  <script data-cfasync="false" type="text/javascript">
    freestar.config.enabled_slots.push({ placementName: "prowrestling_incontent_2", slotId: "prowrestling_incontent_2" });
  </script>
</div></div>
<p>Ospreay said he didn&#8217;t believe Fletcher. He said it could have been two brothers who put aside their differences and fought for the most important championship in pro wrestling. Ospreay said it still could be. He said he knows that Fletcher still loves him deep down. Ospreay said he still loves Fletcher, who yelled at him to stop. Fletcher accused Ospreay of being manipulative. Fletcher said it&#8217;s always been about Ospreay. Fletcher said that he, Mark Davis, and Callum Newman realized it, and one day Ospreay&#8217;s wife will realize it and leave him.</p>
<p>Fletcher said that one day Ospreay&#8217;s son will grow up and he will realize it too. He said that he would be there to let Ospreay&#8217;s son know what kind of man his father is. Fletcher said there would only be hatred at Full Gear, and he would take everything from Ospreay.</p>
<p>Ospreay spoke about how much Fletcher has improved, but he said they are not on equal footing. Ospreay said he won five of their six matches. Ospreay recalled the killer instinct he had to show Jon Moxley and Kenny Omega. He said he would now point that gun at Fletcher. Ospreay said that Fletcher&#8217;s lights would go out. Ospreay said he would stand over the top of Fletcher holding his AEW World Championship. Ospreay said that when it comes to him and Fletcher, he would always have the high ground.</p>
<p>Ospreay tried to say he was on another level, but Fletcher cut him off by slapping him across the face. Fletcher yelled off-mic to show him what he had. Ospreay completed the sentence that Fletcher&#8217;s slap interrupted by simply saying &#8220;level&#8221; before he exited the ring. Fletcher seethed while he watched Ospreay leave&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> Long promos are too WWE. I want matches, matches, and more matches!!! I&#8217;ll bet that the vast majority of fans who made comments like that are raving about how good this promo exchange was. I was frustrated coming out of last week&#8217;s show because I didn&#8217;t think the company had done a good job with the build to Ospreay vs. Fletcher. They changed that with a terrific verbal exchange on the go-home show. To be fair, this segment may have been a little long for some fans, but it was just the latest example of how strong mic work can make a match</p>
<p>A brief video package spotlighted the Kazuchika Okada vs. Adam Copeland match for the AEW International Championship at Full Gear&#8230;</p>
<p>Kofi and Austin Creed made their entrance. Bandido and Brody King were out next, but Kofi and Creed hit them with simultaneous suicide dives. The teams fought at ringside&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>1. Bandido and Brody King vs. Kofi and Austin Creed.</strong> The referee called for the opening bell once a wrestler from each team was inside the ring. The teams continued to fight mostly at ringside before a picture-in-picture break. [C] King performed a suicide dive that took out both opponents on the floor. Kofi and Creed came back by running King into the ring steps. King sold his right shoulder. Bandido dove off the steps onto Kofi and Creed. The teams continued to fight at ringside. Bandido called for King to grab a table. Kofi swung a chair at Bandido, who avoided it. The referee called for the bell.</p>
<p><em>Bandido and Brody King fought Kofi and Austin Creed to a double count-out in 6:45.</em></p>
<p>Afterward, King set up a table on the floor next to the entrance ramp. Security came to separate the teams. Kofi dove off the ramp and hit King with a crossbody block that caused both men to crash through the table. Bandido and Creed fought to the back. Kofi and King got up and wanted to fight more, but security pulled them apart&#8230;</p><div id="prowr-138153294" class="prowr-content-5 prowr-entity-placement" role="region" aria-label="Advertisements"><!-- Tag ID: prowrestling_incontent_3 -->
<div align="center" data-freestar-ad="__336x280 __336x280" id="prowrestling_incontent_3">
  <script data-cfasync="false" type="text/javascript">
    freestar.config.enabled_slots.push({ placementName: "prowrestling_incontent_3", slotId: "prowrestling_incontent_3" });
  </script>
</div></div>
<p>A Veterans Day video package aired. It acknowledged Carlie Bravo, Shawn Dean, Trish Adroa, Bobby Lashley, and Swerve Strickland&#8217;s military backgrounds&#8230; [C]</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> The match was brief, but it was all action. More importantly, it established that things are heated enough between all six wrestlers to justify the Texas Death stipulation.</p>
<p>Footage aired from after Blood &amp; Guts of Renee Paquette in the babyface locker room. AEW Tag Team Champions Jamie Hayter and Alex Windsor bickered with their Full Gear challengers Harley Cameron and Kris Statlander&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> I&#8217;m doing my best to keep up with this fast-paced show, so I&#8217;ll have to go back and watch the women&#8217;s locker room segment again. On a side note, <a href="https://x.com/WrestleTix">WrestleTix</a> listed the venue as being set up for 2,477, with 2,202 tickets distributed. The total number of seats on the map is 5,974. The last time AEW ran the venue, 2,429 tickets were distributed for the October 23, 2024, Dynamite.</p>
<p>Orange Cassidy made his entrance while ring announcer Justin Roberts introduced him. Roderick Strong and Kyle O&#8217;Reilly joined Cassidy on the stage, but they did not accompany him to the ring. Renee Paquette spoke at ringside and noted that everyone was banned from ringside. David Finlay made his entrance to a flat crowd reaction&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>2. Orange Cassidy vs. David Finlay.</strong> Cassidy performed a crossbody block a few minutes into the match, but Finlay caught him and performed a backbreaker before a PIP break. [C] Cassidy bit Finlay&#8217;s forehead and then raked his back, which the broadcast team said was a page out of Jon Moxley&#8217;s playbook. Finlay rolled to the floor and then slid a chair inside the ring. While the referee cleared the chair, Finlay hit Cassidy with his shillelagh and then got the three count.</p>
<p><em>David Finlay beat Orange Cassidy in roughly 10:00.</em></p>
<p><strong>[Hour Two]</strong> Afterward, the referee found the shillelagh, but Finlay denied using it. The broadcast team explained that the referee didn&#8217;t see Finlay use the weapon. Roderick Strong and Kyle O&#8217;Reilly ran out and entered the ring. Austin Gunn and Colten Gunn showed up near the barricade, which distracted Strong and O&#8217;Reilly. Clark Connors showed up and speared Cassidy&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> Referees can only call what they see. Remember this the next time they inevitably go with a finish that contradicts that.</p>
<p>Renee Paquette interviewed Andrade El Idolo on the backstage interview set. He had his framed contract for a shot at the AEW World Championship with him. Andrade said he would make history by becoming the first AEW World Champion, then said it was a promise from him, the Real Latino Man&#8230;</p>
<p>Excalibur hyped the AEW National Championship match&#8230; A Thanksgiving-themed ad featuring AEW wrestlers aired to promote the Thanksgiving Eve edition of Dynamite and the Thanksgiving night edition of Collision&#8230; [C]</p>
<p>Backstage, Lexi Nair interviewed Stokely Hathaway and noted that the winners of the best-of-five match will earn a shot at the AEW Tag Team Titles. Hathaway spoke of the respect between FTR and the Motor City Machine Guns, then spoke about what respect won&#8217;t buy. He said FTR will become the No. 1 contenders&#8230;</p>
<p>Persephone made her entrance with Britt Baker, while her opponent was already in the ring&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>3. CMLL Women&#8217;s Champion Persephone vs. Gypsy Mac in a non-title match.</strong> Britt Baker sat in on commentary. Persephone dominated the match and performed a crucifix bomb that led to the three count.</p>
<p><em>CMLL Women&#8217;s Champion Persephone defeated Gypsy Mac in 1:30 in a non-title match.</em></p>
<p>Afterward, Persephone grabbed a headset and accused Queen Aminata of stealing the TBS Championship&#8230;</p>
<p>Backstage, Renee Paquette interviewed Hangman Page and asked him what changed that the AEW Trios Title match became a Texas Death Match. Page said it&#8217;s the most dangerous thing you can do during your career. He said you walk into the match without knowing whether you will ever walk again.</p>
<p>Page said it&#8217;s not that he&#8217;s afraid of Texas Death; it&#8217;s the &#8220;not understanding.&#8221; He said he told everyone involved not to give Swerve Strickland what he wants, but it&#8217;s not about him anymore. Page introduced Brody King and Bandido and said they want and need Texas Death. Page said he would walk beside his brothers into the mouth of hell.</p>
<p>King said he understands Page&#8217;s hesitation and the feeling of hate isn&#8217;t worth it. King said hate was his worth for years, but Bandido showed him a different way to walk. King said he gets to be the old version of himself at Full Gear. King said a man has to come to peace with the atrocities he&#8217;s willing to commit in a Texas Death Match and pray that a god is willing to forgive him. &#8220;Lucky for me, I don&#8217;t believe in God; I believe in violence,&#8221; King said. Bandido added that their opponents would meet (or need?) their faith, and then made a finger gun&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> It wasn&#8217;t a good call to close with Bandido, but the rest of the promo really put over the danger of a Texas Death match.</p>
<p><strong>4. &#8220;Motor City Machine Guns&#8221; Alex Shelley and Chris Sabin vs. &#8220;FTR&#8221; Dax Harwood and Cash Wheeler (w/Stokely Hathaway) in the fifth and final match of the best-of-five series.</strong> They cut to a PIP break early in the match. [C] After some back-and-forth action, Wheeler stood on the floor and hit Sabin with the ring bell. Harwood covered Sabin for a near fall. &#8220;Ref, you suck,&#8221; a fan yelled right before a PIP break. [C]</p>
<p>Late in the match, Shelley dove off the apron and hit Hathaway with a flying knee. Back in the ring, the Guns hit their finisher on Harwood, but Wheeler broke up the pin. A &#8220;holy shit&#8221; chant broke out. Moments later, Shelley tried to suplex Harwood, but Hathaway tripped him, which led to a near fall. Shelley went after Hathaway, who entered the ring. Shelley followed, but FTR hit him with a Shatter Machine and had him beat, but Sabin broke up the pin.</p>
<p>Sabin put Hathaway down with Cradle Shock. FTR hit Sabin and Shelley with spike piledrivers. Harwood covered Shelley, who kicked out at the last moment. Justin Roberts announced that there was one minute remaining in the time limit. Nothing happened for 30 seconds. FTR went for a Shatter Machine, but Shelley avoided it, rolled up Harwood, and pinned him.</p>
<p><em>&#8220;Motor City Machine Guns&#8221; Alex Shelley and Chris Sabin defeated &#8220;FTR&#8221; Dax Harwood and Cash Wheeler in roughly 19:50 in the fifth and final match of the best-of-five series to earn a shot at the AEW Tag Team Titles.</em></p>
<p>Afterward, the fans applauded as the teams got to their feet and shook hands while Hathaway watched from the floor&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> A very good match to end the strong best-of-five series. I could have done without the wrestlers kicking out of damn near everything, especially the ring bell shot. For that matter, the time limit draw tease felt silly. Why would the last match of the series have a 20-minute time limit? Better yet, why would the final match have a 20-minute time limit when the first match of the series went just over 26 minutes? Those complaints aside, it was cool to see these teams share the ring.</p>
<p>A montage of still shots was shown of AEW&#8217;s past events in the Salt Lake City area&#8230; Entrances for the AEW National Championship match took place&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>5. Tommaso Ciampa vs. Mike Bailey for the AEW National Championship.</strong> A few minutes into the match, Ciampa hit Willow&#8217;s Bell. Bailey rolled to the floor. Ciampa followed and hit a running knee strike that drove Bailey&#8217;s head into the ring steps. Bailey bled from the forehead before a PIP break. [C]</p>
<p>Bailey was on the ropes when Ciampa was stuck in the tree of woe. Bailey threw kicks while seated on the top turnbuckle until Ciampa bit his foot. Bailey came back and hit the Ultima Weapon for a near fall. Ciampa stood on the middle rope and hit an Avalanche Project Ciampa for a near fall. Ciampa lowered his kneepad and drilled Bailey with a running knee strike for another near fall. Ciampa acted stunned. Ciampa grabbed Bailey, who slapped him and then threw his mouthguard at him.</p>
<p>[Hour Three] Ciampa hit another running knee strike and then pinned Bailey.</p>
<p>Tommaso Ciampa defeated Mike Bailey in 15:55 to retain the AEW National Championship.</p>
<p>After the match, Ilja Dragunov made his entrance while Ciampa clutched his title belt. Dragunov entered the ring dressed in non-wrestling attire and played to the crowd. Dragunov went face-to-face with Ciampa, who jawed at him. Dragunov shoved him back and then pointed to the big screen, which had a graphic for the two of them meeting for the AEW National Championship at Full Gear. The fans chanted &#8220;AEW.&#8221; Ciampa extended his hand. When Dragunov reached for the handshake, Ciampa flipped him off and left the ring&#8230; [C]</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> If nothing else, I guess the go-home block is preparing viewers for wrestlers kicking out of everything at Full Gear. But while I wish they would pull back on the over-the-top near falls, the live crowd popped big for all of them. And this was a really good match despite my quibbles. The post-match angle was simple, but that&#8217;s all it needed to be. Ciampa vs. Dragunov is a great addition to the Full Gear lineup. This would have been a logical point to end Dynamite before they roll into Collision, but Tony Khan thinks we need more of the A-show.</p>
<p>Jay White and Mercedes Mone made their entrances via the stage and were accompanied by several members of The Cut. Jon Moxley and Marina Shafir entered through the crowd&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>6. AEW Women’s Champion Mercedes Mone and Jay White vs. Marina Shafir and AEW Continental Champion Jon Moxley in a mixed tag match.</strong> The referee ejected all of The Cut wrestlers from ringside before calling for the opening bell. This wasn&#8217;t fought under traditional mixed tag rules, as White performed a backbreaker on Shafir for a near fall before a PIP break. [C]</p>
<p>Excalibur ran through the Collision lineup and added Mistico and Mascara Dorada vs. &#8220;The Swirl&#8221; Blake Christian and Lee Johnson for the ROH Tag Team Titles.</p>
<p>Moxley performed a piledriver on White, whose head ended up on Moxley&#8217;s legs and nowhere near the mat, for a near fall. Moxley put White in the Bulldog Choke until Mone kicked Moxley. Mone slapped Moxley, who grabbed her until White clipped his leg.</p>
<p>Moments later, Mone put Moxley in the Statementmaker while Shafir put White in a triangle. The broadcast team noted that neither woman was legal, so the submission holds could not end the match. Once they released the holds, Moxley and Shafir took turns hitting White with running strikes in a corner of the ring. Mone hit Moxley with a Codebreaker.</p>
<p>White put Shafir down with a Blade Runner. Mone low-blowed Moxley, who recovered and then put her down with a cutter. White performed a snap dragon suplex on Moxley, who stood right up and responded with a lariat. All four wrestlers were down. The men rolled to the floor. Mone got up and hit the Moneymaker on Shafir, who countered into the Brutalizer for the submission win.</p>
<p><em>Marina Shafir and Jon Moxley beat Mercedes Mone and Jay White in 14:05.</em></p>
<p>Shafir and Moxley celebrated their win. Shafir returned to the ring to go to the ropes, but Mone hit her from behind and applied the Statementmaker. The screen went black for a second to end Dynamite.</p>
<p>Collision started with Austin Gunn, Colten Gunn, Ace Austin, David Finlay, and Clark Connors entering the ring and attacking Moxley while Mone kept Shafir locked in the submission hold.</p>
<p>Roderick Strong and Kyle O&#8217;Reilly walked slowly down the ramp and got the attention of the idiot heels. Orange Cassidy, who had his ribs wrapped, entered the ring behind the Cut wrestlers and attacked them. Mone fled to ringside. Strong and O&#8217;Reilly joined Cassidy in attacking the Cut. O&#8217;Reilly took Colten down and tried to apply the ankle lock, but Colten&#8217;s allies pulled him to ringside. Moxley and Cassidy shook hands in the ring. At ringside, Mone hit Shafir with the AEW Women&#8217;s Championship belt&#8230;</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Powell&#8217;s POV:</strong></span> Nothing screams AEW Collision quite like Roderick Strong and Kyle O&#8217;Reilly show up. Shafir forcing Mone to submit to Pac&#8217;s Brutalizer was a nice touch. The fans would pop huge if she used that hold to win the title on Saturday. I&#8217;m looking forward to that match. I can&#8217;t really say the same for Anarchy in the Arena, but it will probably have enough fun moments to win me over.</p>
<p>Backstage, &#8220;The Triangle of Madness&#8221; Thekla, Julia Hart, and Skye Blue delivered a promo. Thekla said Hart had barbed wire shoved in her mouth during the Blood &amp; Guts match. Thekla asked if they whined or complained. She answered her own question by saying no. She said they loved it because they knew payback would be so much worse. Blue said she was covered in blood all night and all morning &#8220;because of the violent little thing that I am.&#8221; Blue spoke about her TBS Championship three-way. Hart said first Aminata, and then every woman in the Blood &amp; Guts match will feel like she did. &#8220;Uh oh, you bitches are in trouble now,&#8221; Thekla said to close&#8230;</p>
<p>The entrances for the trios match took place&#8230;</p>
<p><strong>7. Jack Perry and AEW Tag Team Champions &#8220;The Young Bucks&#8221; Matt Jackson and Nick Jackson vs. Kevin Knight, Brian Cage, and El Clon.</strong> Don Callis did not accompany his team to ringside. Walker Stewart sat in on commentary. Perry and the Bucks were standing tall while their opponents were down. [C]</p>
